- How would you propagate policy updates across a multi-instance deployment?
- How would you test the policy engine and TTL cache behavior?
- How would you handle token revocation and clock skew in this design?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world setups use multiple IdPs; token replay and cross-provider binding are critical issues.

## Key Concepts
- JWKS caching and key rotation per provider
- Replay protection with jti in distributed cache
- Token binding via CNF and mTLS
- Revocation propagation and token lifecycle

## Code Example
```javascript
function verifyJwt(token, provider) {
  const key = getJwksKey(provider, token.kid);
  const payload = jwtVerify(token, key);
  if (Date.now() >= payload.exp * 1000) throw new Error('expired');
  if (redis.exists(`jti:${payload.jti}`)) throw new Error('replay');
  redis.set(`jti:${payload.jti}`, 1, 'EX', payload.exp - now);
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle JWKS rotation events?
- How would you monitor and debug cross-provider revocation flows?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of practical ES+CQRS integration across microservices with a lightweight saga.

## Key Concepts
- Event Sourcing: immutable event log
- CQRS: separate read model for queries
- Saga/Orchestrator: cross-service workflow with compensations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch
function handleEvent(event) {
  switch (event.type) {
    case 'PostCreated':
      publish('ModerationRequested', { postId: event.data.postId });
      break;
    case 'ModerationResult':
      if (event.data.result === 'Approved') {
        publish('PostPublished', { postId: event.data.postId });
        publish('NotifyFollowers', { postId: event.data.postId });
      } else {
        publish('PostRejected', { postId: event.data.postId, reason: event.data.reason });
      }
      break;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement idempotent event processing in the Moderation service?
- What are the trade-offs of using a separate read model vs. a consolidated repository for listings of visible posts?

