- How would you ensure exactly-once processing for the tenant outbox?
- How would you test failure injection and crash recovery in this Saga?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle multi-tenant token flows with dynamic metadata sources and replay protection, a common real-world requirement.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC/SAML validation paths, JWKS/SAML metadata fetch with caching
- Per-tenant audience checks and nonce-based replay protection
- Short-lived internal JWT with tenant and scopes; caching for performance

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo: tenant-aware JWKS fetch with cache
async function getTenantKeys(tenant) {
  const cached = cache.get(tenant);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const keys = await fetch(tenant.jwks_uri).then(r => r.json());
  cache.set(tenant, keys, 30000); // 30s
  return keys;
}
```

